CVE-2022-0847 is a kernel vulnerability related to the way the Linux kernel handles memory allocation for pipes. The vulnerability is due to a flaw in the way the kernel handles the `pipe_buf_get` function, which can lead to a use-after-free scenario when accessing the pipe buffer.

